# redox-os/bootloader @ f3d9261: framebuffer bit depth + boot menu timeout
#
# Target repository : https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/bootloader.git
# Base commit       : f3d9261 (master, 2026-11)
# Reason            : UEFI GOP does not guarantee a 32-bit linear framebuffer.
#                     U-Boot v2021.07 formats the Rockchip VOP as RGB565 for
#                     the eDP panel of the Pinebook Pro (rk_vop.c forces
#                     VIDEO_BPP16 for VOP_MODE_EDP) and reports the surface
#                     with PixelBitMask (0xf800/0x07e0/0x001f); gop_set_mode
#                     accepts only mode 0, so the depth cannot be changed.
#
#                     OsVideoMode now carries bpp, derived after SetMode from
#                     Mode.Info.PixelFormat: 32 for the two 8-bit-per-channel
#                     formats, and the highest set bit of the R/G/B bit masks
#                     for PixelBitMask (0xffff -> 16). The value is written to
#                     the boot environment as FRAMEBUFFER_BPP (same blob as
#                     FRAMEBUFFER_STRIDE, so init passes it to services) and
#                     the framebuffer is mapped with the real size. Unknown
#                     formats export 0, which consumers treat as 32bpp; VBE
#                     keeps 32 (it only accepts 32-bit modes).
#
#                     The mode menu used to block in `get_key()`, so a machine
#                     with no keyboard attached (a headless QEMU run, or the
#                     Pinebook Pro before the USB driver works) never booted.
#                     `Os` gained `get_key_timeout(ms)`, defaulting to the old
#                     blocking `get_key()`; the UEFI implementation polls the
#                     non-blocking `ReadKeyStroke` against a deadline taken from
#                     `RuntimeServices.GetTime`. That clock is dead on boards
#                     without an RTC driver (no RK808 support in the installed
#                     U-Boot), so the deadline is only trusted once the clock
#                     has been seen to tick; a constant or failing clock falls
#                     back to a bounded spin. `select_mode` now waits 3 s, then
#                     boots the highlighted mode, and the hint says so.
#
# Apply from the repo root:  git apply <this file>
